# Build context exclusions.
#
# The first entry is not housekeeping. This project lives on an exFAT volume, so
# every file gets a macOS AppleDouble sidecar (`._name`). The Docker file sender
# tries to read their extended attributes, the filesystem refuses, and the whole
# build aborts before the first instruction:
#
#   failed to solve: failed to read dockerfile: error from sender:
#   failed to xattr /…/._.chart-data-TJiVp4: operation not permitted
#
# Nothing below is needed by either build stage. The CSS stage copies exactly the
# files it needs (package.json, tailwind.config.js, tailwind/, core/templates/),
# and the app stage installs from requirements/prod.txt and then copies the
# application. Tests, docs, the real .env, the virtualenv and all local build
# state stay out of the image.

# --- exFAT / macOS -------------------------------------------------------------
._*
.DS_Store
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- Local state and secrets ---------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.git
.gitignore
.ignore
.venv
node_modules
staticfiles
artifacts
outputs
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
__pycache__
*.py[cod]

# --- Not part of the runtime image --------------------------------------------
tests/
docs/
scripts/
deploy/
handoff*.md
BUILD_STATUS.md
QA_REPORT.md
roomreserveapp*.md
roomreserveapp*.pdf
deepseek-v3-build-loop.md
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.png
compose*.yaml
pyproject.toml
